From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 06:04:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mend dead keys, swallowed clicks, and a search run again for
 nothing

Three small faults in changes this branch made itself, two found by
the review of the whole branch and one by the review of the
double-click change.

Go to Folder, called with the keyboard in the filter field of an open
Smart Folder and confirmed with Return, left the keys dead until
something was clicked: the arrow keys and typing did nothing, nor did
Cmd+F and the other shortcuts the window itself handles. Going to the
folder ends the Smart Folder's search, and its filter bar goes with
it. The dialog then closed and gave the keyboard back to what had it
when the dialog opened, the bar's field, which was no longer drawn.
The net for a keyboard that is lost didn't act: what stopped being
drawn with the keyboard was the dialog, which is no part of the
browser, and GPUI reports nothing lost when the keyboard then lands on
a field that isn't drawn. The same happened when `fff gui` or a second
launch sent the window somewhere else with a dialog open over that
field. As a frame is drawn, a browser now looks whether its filter
field has the keyboard with its bar away, and gives the keyboard to
its files. A dialog that leaves the bar where it is still gives the
field the keyboard back.

Choosing Relevance again in a search's Sort menu, where it is the
checked item, turned around a direction that Relevance doesn't have.
The menu then showed Descending checked, with both directions off, and
a list whose items a sort may choose was searched again. It now does
nothing, as choosing the direction a list already has does.

After a double-click on a button under the file area's message, such
as Search This Computer, every further click made without a pause or a
move of the mouse was ignored: a double-click on the result that had
come under the pointer opened nothing, for as long as the clicking
went on. The guard for the second click of that double-click stopped
every press the system counted second or later, until one it counted
first. It now stops that one press only, and has the views count it as
a press they left alone, so the click after it selects the result and
the one after that opens it, as after a double-click on a dialog's
button. When it is the next button that came under the pointer, the
click after the double-click presses it. The guard stays, although the
views by now leave such a second click alone on an item themselves:
they don't on the next button or on a group's header.

docs/manual.md: the Sort By line says that Relevance, chosen again,
has no order to reverse.

Changelog: none (fixes a fault in an unreleased change).

